# Clickable resource links in chat

When mentioning any resource in chat, give a **direct, clickable link** — not bare
identifiers, shortened paths, or references without a destination.

## Always link

- **URLs** — full scheme and path in markdown links; do not elide segments.
- **Repository files** — link the full path, e.g.
  [`skills/prepare-pr/SKILL.md`](skills/prepare-pr/SKILL.md).
- **GitHub** — issues, pull requests, commits, and files as full URLs.
- **Linear** — issues and projects as full workspace URLs.
- **Docs, plans, ADRs, skills, rules** — link the file or page when you reference it.

## Format

- Prefer `[label](full-url-or-path)`.
- Pair ids with titles when both are known (e.g. `[MR-529: Forum layout fix](https://linear.app/...)`).
- Use code citations for excerpts; link the file when referencing it without a block.

## Do not

- Name a URL, file, issue, or doc without linking when the location is known.
- Truncate URLs or paths for brevity.
- Make the user search for something you can link directly.

Apply in chat and human-facing artifacts (PR bodies, plans, summaries). Skip link
decoration inside code identifiers and verbatim quoted text.

## On-disk artifacts (sibling rule)

Per-file markdown links for previews, exports, logs, evidence JSON, and reports are
covered by [`artifact-output-links.mdc`](artifact-output-links.mdc) (and repo
`.cursor/rules/artifact-output-links.mdc` / `AGENTS.md` when in a repo). This rule
covers general clickable resources — not the artifact-output checklist.
